        "description": "KMS key policy grants administrative actions to non-administrator principals. Unauthorized principals can disable the key, schedule deletion, or modify the key policy.",
        "action": "Restrict key administration statements to designated key administrator roles. Separate key usage (Encrypt/Decrypt) from key administration (Create*/Put*/Disable*/Schedule*) in the key policy. Use separate statements with distinct principals for usage and administration.",
        "example": "{\n  \"cryptography\": {\n    \"kind\": \"key\",\n    \"policy\": {\n      \"admin_actions_broadly_granted\": false\n    }\n  }\n}\n"
